  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"proteus\" %}\n{% set version = \"1.8.3\" %}\n{% set build = 21 %}\n{% set sha256 = \"315f0600044e2ad86592c248a9a4ca87dc58c1d678af2c27a9ddde802b555618\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  fn: proteus-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  url: https://github.com/erdc/proteus/archive/{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: {{ sha256 }}\n  patches:\n    # v1.8.3's setup.py hard-codes -mavx (x86-only) for MeshSmoothing and\n    # cMoveMeshMonitor, which fails outright on any non-x86 target (\"error:\n    # unrecognized command-line option '-mavx'\" on linux-aarch64;\n    # \"unsupported option '-mavx' for target arm64-apple-darwin...\" on\n    # osx-arm64). Fixed upstream after this release (erdc/proteus commit\n    # 13d526b1) but not yet in a new tag. conda-build's arm64/aarch64\n    # selectors are OS-specific names for the same architecture (osx uses\n    # \"arm64\", linux uses \"aarch64\"), so both are needed here.\n    - fix-arm64-avx.patch  # [(osx and arm64) or (linux and aarch64)]\n    # xtensor 0.27.1 reorganized its headers into subdirectories by\n    # category -- xio.hpp -> io/xio.hpp, xarray.hpp -> containers/\n    # xarray.hpp, xview.hpp -> views/xview.hpp, xfixed.hpp -> containers/\n    # xfixed.hpp (confirmed against the actual 0.27.1 source tree; all\n    # four old paths 404). Only matters on linux-aarch64, where the\n    # recipe's own xtensor pin above is relaxed to >=0.27.1 (no older\n    # xtensor-python builds exist for that platform at all) -- every\n    # other platform stays on the old xtensor pin and doesn't need this.\n    # Patches every proteus header that includes any of these four\n    # (ArgumentsDict.h, RANS2P.h, RANS2P2D.h) -- confirmed exhaustive via\n    # a full grep of the source tree for xtensor/* includes.\n    - fix-linux-aarch64-xio-path.patch  # [linux and aarch64]\n    # The newer xtensor/xtl required on linux-aarch64 (see above) uses\n    # both std::conjunction (C++17) and C++20 `concept` syntax\n    # unconditionally in its headers -- but every extension that calls\n    # get_xtensor_include() (exactly the 35 that hard-code -std=c++14)\n    # fails with \"'conjunction' is not a member of 'std'\" and then, once\n    # bumped only to C++17, \"'concept' does not name a type\". Bump those\n    # 35 '-std=c++14' occurrences straight to '-std=c++20' instead.\n    # Scoped to linux-aarch64 only, same as the two patches above.\n    - fix-linux-aarch64-cxx20.patch  # [linux and aarch64]\n\nbuild:\n  number: {{ build }}\n  skip: true  # [win]\n  # scorec has no openmpi build on osx-arm64 (openmpi's mpicc/mpicxx are\n  # real compiled binaries that can't execute under cross-compilation from\n  # an osx-64 build host, unlike mpich's portable shell-script wrappers --\n  # see scorec-feedstock recipe). Since proteus unconditionally requires\n  # both scorec and {{ mpi }}, the openmpi variant can never solve here.\n  skip: true  # [osx and arm64 and mpi == \"openmpi\"]\n  {% set mpi_prefix = \"mpi_\" + mpi %}\n  string: {{ mpi_prefix }}_h{{ PKG_HASH }}_{{ build }}\n  run_exports:\n    - {{ name }} * {{ mpi_prefix }}_*\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - {{ compiler('c') }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - {{ compiler('fortran') }}\n    - make\n    # Needed for cross-compiled builds (osx-arm64 built from an osx-64\n    # host): without a build-platform python + cross-python's sysconfig\n    # shim, there is no usable \"python\"/\"$PYTHON\" to run setup.py at all\n    # -- $PREFIX/bin/python is a real arm64 binary that can't execute on\n    # the x86_64 build machine (\"Bad CPU type in executable\"). See\n    # h5py-feedstock's recipe for the same pattern.\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cython >=3                             # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - numpy >=1.25.1                         # [build_platform != target_platform]\n  host:\n    - setuptools\n    - cython >=3\n    - pybind11\n    - pip\n    - metis\n    - {{ mpi }}\n    - numpy >=1.25.1\n    # Unpinned \"openblas\" lets the solver satisfy it with the ancient\n    # 0.3.4 ABI-compatibility-shim build conda-forge keeps around for its\n    # generic libblas/liblapack dispatch layer -- that build doesn't\n    # actually use the libgfortran5 run_exports pulls in, so anything\n    # linking it (proteus's superluWrappers extension, in particular)\n    # fails at import time with \"libgfortran.so.3: cannot open shared\n    # object file\" since only libgfortran.so.5 is provided. A lower\n    # bound is enough to keep the solver on a real, current build.\n    - openblas >=0.3.20\n    - parmetis\n    - petsc4py\n    - petsc\n    # real_*, not complex_*: proteus's C++ is built with -DPETSC_SKIP_COMPLEX\n    # and assumes real PETSC_SCALAR throughout. Without this filter the\n    # solver is free to pick either scalar variant. Kept as a separate entry\n    # (like hdf5's mpi_prefix filter below) rather than replacing the bare\n    # \"petsc\" line above, since conda-build's variant-based version pinning\n    # (from conda_build_config.yaml) is only applied to a literal bare\n    # package name in the recipe text.\n    #\n    # petsc4py itself has no equivalent \"real_*\"/\"complex_*\" build string\n    # (its own recipe.yaml has no `build.string` override, just a generic\n    # hash) -- it's already correctly filtered indirectly, since its own\n    # host requirement is `petsc ${version_xy}.* ${scalar}_*`, so once\n    # petsc itself is pinned to real_* here, any petsc4py built against\n    # complex petsc becomes unsatisfiable on its own.\n    - petsc * real_*\n    - python\n    # Upper bound: scorec >=3 renamed/restructured its core PCU parallel-\n    # communication API to take an explicit PCU_t handle on every call\n    # (previously global, zero-argument functions) -- see SCOREC/core PR\n    # #433 (\"pcu-object-breaking\"). proteus's MeshAdaptPUMI C++ glue code\n    # calls the old global-style API directly across ~150 sites in 7\n    # files and hasn't been ported yet. Without this pin the solver is\n    # free to float proteus onto an incompatible scorec build as soon as\n    # one lands on conda-forge (see conda-forge/scorec-feedstock#27).\n    - scorec >=2.2.8,<3\n    - triangle\n    - superlu\n    - superlu_dist\n    - pychrono >=9,<10\n    - mpi4py\n    # include-paths changed in 0.25. linux-aarch64 only ever had\n    # xtensor-python 0.29.0 built (no older builds exist for that platform\n    # at all), which pulls in xtensor >=0.27.1 -- unsatisfiable against the\n    # <0.26 pin below, so relax it there specifically rather than for\n    # every platform. proteus's only xtensor usage is xt::pyarray<T> as a\n    # plain function-parameter type in ADR.h (xtensor-python/pyarray.hpp),\n    # which is unchanged in 0.29.0, so this is expected to compile fine.\n    - xtensor <0.26  # [not (linux and aarch64)]\n    - xtensor >=0.27.1,<0.28.0a0  # [linux and aarch64]\n    - xtensor-python\n    - eigen\n    # pinning from conda_build_config and build pinning from {{ mpi_prefix }}\n    - hdf5\n    - hdf5 * {{ mpi_prefix }}_*\n  run:\n    - mpi4py\n    - scipy\n    - tetgen\n    - triangle\n    - ncurses\n    - pychrono >=9,<10\n    - scorec >=2.2.8,<3\n    - python 3\n    - {{ pin_compatible('openblas', max_pin='x.x') }}\n    - {{ pin_compatible('petsc4py', max_pin='x.x') }}\n    - {{ pin_compatible('cython', max_pin='x.x') }}\n    # pinning from conda_build_config and build pinning from {{ mpi_prefix }}\n    - hdf5\n    - hdf5 * {{ mpi_prefix }}_*\n    - h5py\n    - h5py * {{ mpi_prefix }}_*\ntest:\n  imports:\n    - proteus\n  source_files:\n    - test\n  requires:\n    - pytest\n    - pytest-forked\n    - matplotlib-base\n  commands:\n    - pytest -v test/ci/test_meshPartitionFromTetgenFiles.py\n\nabout:\n  home: http://proteustoolkit.org\n  license: MIT\n  license_family: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE.md\n  summary: Proteus is a Python package for rapidly developing computer models and numerical methods.\n  dev_url: https://github.com/erdc/proteus\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - davidbrochart\n    - SylvainCorlay\n    - martinRenou\n    - zhang-alvin\n    - jan-janssen\n    - cekees\n",
